d=base('build_evidence_museum','The evidence museum','Review • Fossils, soils and light',39,'Use evidence to correct museum labels about fossils, soils and light.',[('fossil','Preserved remains or traces of ancient life.'),('soil','A mixture that includes mineral and organic material.'),('reflect','Send arriving light back from a surface.'),('evidence','Information that supports or challenges an idea.')],['Use a clue from each science strand.','Correct an inaccurate exhibit label.','State one thing the evidence cannot tell us.'],['Fossils can preserve evidence of past living things.','Soils contain different materials.','Light must reach an eye for sight.'],[('Every stone is a fossil.','A fossil is preserved evidence of past life; a stone alone need not contain this evidence.','Ask what evidence of life is present.'),('Soil is only tiny rock.','Soil also contains organic matter and spaces with air or water.','Ask which card shows a non-mineral component.'),('An eye lights up an exhibit.','Light enters the eye from the lit exhibit.','Trace the arrow at the eye.')],[BGS])
