d=base('build_plant_system_jobs','The plant-system service desk','Summer 1 • Explain how the parts work together',31,'Explain how roots, stem, leaves and flowers contribute to the life of a flowering plant.',[('absorb','Take in a substance, such as water.'),('mineral nutrient','A substance needed in small amounts for growth.'),('photosynthesis','Making sugars using light energy.'),('seed','A structure containing a young plant and food reserves.')],['Match each main part to a useful job.','Explain one connection between parts.','Distinguish mineral uptake from making sugars.'],['Identify roots, stem, leaves and flower.','Plants require water.'],[('Roots eat soil as food.','Roots absorb water and dissolved minerals; green parts make sugars using light.','Ask where sugars are made and where water enters.'),('The stem only holds the flower.','It supports parts and contains transport pathways.','Ask how root-absorbed water reaches leaves.'),('Flowers exist only to look attractive.','They take part in reproduction and can lead to seed formation.','Ask what a successfully fertilised flower can develop into.')],[SAPS,WATER_SOURCE])
jobcards=[('A • Roots','Anchor the plant. Absorb water and dissolved mineral nutrients.'),('B • Stem','Supports leaves and flowers. Contains pathways transporting water and other substances.'),('C • Green leaves','Use light energy, water and carbon dioxide from air to make sugars.'),('D • Flowers','Take part in reproduction. After successful pollination and fertilisation, seeds can form.'),('E • Service case','A plant’s leaves are shaded by a box. Its roots still have water; the box prevents light reaching the leaves.'),('F • Connection case','Water has entered the roots. It still needs a pathway through the stem to reach the leaves.')]
d['slides']=[slide('Opening',2,'Can one plant part do every job?',['Follow the work through the whole plant.'],'Do not anthropomorphise a service desk into intention: “jobs” means biological functions.'),slide('Retrieval',3,'Name the part before its function',['1. Which part branches below soil?','2. Which part holds leaves?','3. Which structure can form seeds?'],'1 roots. 2 stem. 3 flowers take part in seed formation. Accept an emerging answer without requiring pollination detail.'),slide('I do',7,'I connect entry to transport',['Roots take in water and minerals.','The stem contains transport pathways.'],'Think aloud: “Water enters through the roots, but the leaves are higher up. I need a connecting pathway. Naming roots alone does not explain arrival at leaves.” Roots also anchor; arrows show selected water movement.',visual=rootjob),slide('I do',0,'I distinguish materials from sugar-making',['Light supplies energy.','Green leaves make sugars.','Minerals are not ready-made food.'],'Shares I do time. Think aloud: “I see water arriving, but sugar-making also needs light and carbon dioxide from air. Soil is not a meal the roots eat.” Oxygen is also produced; the simplified diagram focuses on the inputs and sugar output.',visual=leafjob),slide('I do',0,'I give flowers a biological function',['Flowers take part in reproduction.','Seeds can form after fertilisation.'],'Shares I do time. Think aloud: “A bright colour may help attract some pollinators, but it is not the whole function. I connect the flower with forming seeds.” Not every flower succeeds; not all flowers are bright or insect-pollinated.',visual=flowerjob),slide('We do',4,'The service desk sorts the jobs',['Use A–D.','Connect each part to a function.','Explain one connection to another part.'],'W1: roots absorb/anchor; stem supports/transports; green leaves make sugars; flowers reproduction/seeds. Roles: explainer, evidence checker, connector. Rotate once.',table=table(['What must happen?','Which part helps?'],[['Water enters from soil','Choose from A–D'],['Water reaches a leaf','Choose from A–D'],['Sugars are made in light','Choose from A–D'],['Seeds form','Choose from A–D']],'Functional matching; no live plant damage')),slide('We do',4,'A repair must address the missing input',['Read E and F.','Choose a useful explanation.','Say why an unrelated repair fails.'],'W2: E needs suitable light reaching leaves; more minerals alone cannot replace light. F needs transport through the stem. Never damage or deliberately shade a class plant to act out a fault.',reveal='A connected system needs suitable inputs and working pathways.'),slide('Hinge',3,'Which account explains plant nutrition?',['Look for both making and absorbing.'],'Correct first option. If soil-food appears, revisit leafjob alongside rootjob.',options=opts([('Roots absorb water and minerals; green leaves make sugars using light.',True,'This distinguishes uptake from sugar-making.'),('Roots eat soil, so leaves have no role.',False,'Minerals and soil are not the plant’s ready-made sugars.'),('Flowers pump all water from the soil.',False,'Roots take in water, which travels through stem pathways.')]))]
d['interactive']=dict(title='Choose the useful plant-system explanation',intro='Use service cards A–F. Predict a function or repair, reveal the diagram, then explain the connection.',slideIndex=5,steps=[step('Water enters from soil. Which part takes it in?',[('Roots',True,'Roots absorb water and dissolved mineral nutrients.'),('Petals',False,'Petals are not the main soil-water entry route.')],rootjob,'The stem then provides transport pathways towards leaves.'),step('In E, leaves receive no light. Will extra minerals replace light?',[('No',True,'Minerals do not supply the light energy required for photosynthesis.'),('Yes',False,'Different requirements cannot simply replace one another.')],leafjob,'Restore suitable light; water and minerals remain necessary too.'),step('Which job explains flowers beyond appearance?',[('They take part in reproduction and seed formation',True,'Successful fertilisation can lead to seeds.'),('They are the only water-absorbing part',False,'Roots are the main entry point from soil.')],flowerjob,'Flowers support reproduction; not every flower forms seeds successfully.')])
d['pupilPages']=[page('Shared evidence • Plant-system cards','Use these biological function cards. The service cases are fictional; do not damage plants.',[cards(jobcards),resp('W1. Choose two parts and explain how their jobs connect.',2),resp('W2. Which input is missing in E? Why will extra minerals not replace it?',2)]),page('Route 1 • Match useful jobs','Word bank: roots / stem / leaves / flowers.',[resp('S1. Which part absorbs water from soil?',2),resp('S2. Which part connects roots to leaves and transports water?',2),resp('S3. Which green parts make sugars using light?',2),resp('S4. Which parts take part in making seeds?',2),choices('S5. Mineral nutrients are...',['Needed substances taken in with water.','Ready-made sugar meals eaten from soil.'])]),page('Route 2 • Write the service guide','Use a part name, a function and a reason.',[resp('M1. Explain how roots and stem help water reach a leaf.',3),resp('M2. Explain why E needs light as well as water.',3),resp('M3. Give two jobs of the stem.',2),resp('M4. Correct “flowers only make the plant look colourful”.',3)]),page('Route 3 • Review a proposed repair','A pupil says: “The shaded plant has water, so giving it twice as many minerals will replace the missing light.”',[resp('T1. Explain the mistake using card C.',3),resp('T2. Propose a repair that addresses the missing input.',2),resp('T3. Explain why roots alone cannot account for water reaching leaves.',3),resp('T4. Must every flower become a seed-bearing fruit? Use a careful sentence.',3)])]
end(d,['Match parts and functions.','Explain the connected system.','Review a proposed repair.'],'Use the same objective across routes. A successful connection includes an entry point and transport, or a photosynthesis input and sugar-making. Do not demand the full photosynthesis equation.','Which connection made our explanation stronger?','Parts have different functions and work together; water uptake is different from making sugars.',['Which part absorbs water from soil?','Where do green plants make sugars using light?','What do flowers help the plant do?'],[('Retrieval 1–3','1 roots. 2 stem. 3 flowers through reproduction and seed formation.'),('We do W1–W2','W1 roots take in water and stem carries it towards leaves; or stem supports leaves that receive light. Water entry roots; water transport stem; sugar-making green leaves; seed formation flowers. W2 light is missing; minerals cannot replace light energy.'),('Hinge','First option correct. The second treats soil as ready-made food; the third assigns root uptake to flowers.'),('S1–S5','S1 roots. S2 stem. S3 green leaves. S4 flowers. S5 needed substances taken in with water.'),('M1–M4','M1 roots absorb water, which travels through pathways in the stem to leaves. M2 light energy is needed to make sugars from water and carbon dioxide; water alone is insufficient. M3 supports leaves/flowers and transports substances. M4 flowers take part in reproduction and can lead to seeds.'),('T1–T4','T1 minerals do not replace the light energy needed for photosynthesis. T2 allow suitable light to reach leaves while maintaining other needs. T3 a connected stem pathway carries water beyond the roots. T4 no; seed development depends on successful reproductive processes and other suitable conditions.'),('Exit E1–E3','E1 roots. E2 green leaves and other photosynthetic green tissues; leaves sufficient for core. E3 reproduce/form seeds.')],['Secure core: four correct part-function links and one accurate connection. If a pupil says food comes from soil, contrast the labelled sugar output with root water/mineral uptake.'])

# 4: growth needs clinic, with height explicitly separated from healthy growth.
needs=vis('Requirements work together','A growing green plant receives light energy, water and mineral nutrients, and exchanges gases with air. Appropriate temperature and space also matter. Amounts vary by species and conditions.',plant_e(flower=False)+[tx(40,40,300,65,'Light energy',30,True),line(235,100,360,215,GOLD),tx(675,75,285,100,'Air around\nthe plant',29,True),line(695,175,560,230,BLUE),tx(40,360,245,120,'Water + dissolved\nmineral nutrients',27),line(260,445,380,450,WATER),tx(665,310,280,140,'Suitable warmth\nand enough space',29,True),tx(35,520,925,35,'More is not always better. Requirements vary.',25,True)])
