d=base('build_water_path_detectives','The water-path detectives','Summer 1 • Trace movement and respect the evidence',35,'Explain the root–stem–leaf water pathway and use dye evidence to identify internal transport in a cut shoot.',[('transport','Movement of a substance from one place to another.'),('xylem','Plant pathways that carry water and dissolved minerals.'),('tracer','A marker used to help follow movement.'),('water vapour','Water in its gas state.')],['Trace soil water through roots and stem to leaves.','Explain what coloured internal pathways support.','State a limit of a rootless demonstration.'],['Roots absorb water and minerals.','Stems contain transport pathways.'],[('Water mainly travels up the outside of the stem.','The dye comparison can reveal internal water-carrying pathways.','Ask where the adult-cut section shows colour.'),('A cut shoot proves how roots absorb water.','The cut shoot has no roots; it gives evidence about transport above the cut.','Ask whether roots are present in the setup.'),('Any falling water level proves every lost drop entered the plant.','Water can also evaporate from a container.','Compare a cup without a plant.')],[WATER_SOURCE,CELERY,SAPS])
